Z||000014||sluppy123||02-05-2001||09:19 PM||||Here's some Pics of the Gauges.<P> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=247832&a=11172186&p=40186187&Sequence=0"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=247832&a=11172186&p=40186423&Sequence=0"> <P><BR>I've Had no second thoughts about ditching the fuzzy crap on the firewall, I've always thought it looked cheap. Just be careful when you recover the panel. Don't cut the edges to close where it meets the center console, If you do you will see a gap around it.<P>Here's my CD changer. Now you see it.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=247832&a=11172186&p=40189875&Sequence=0"> <P>Now you Don't.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=247832&a=11172186&p=40189805&Sequence=0"> ||||reg||10
Z||000015||sluppy123||02-05-2001||09:33 PM||||Monkeyman- I had my doubts about doing the headliner in vinyl, but once i started working with it the more I thought it might be possible. I used a hairdryer to help soften it and to help smooth out some of the wrinkles. For glue I used 3M Foam Fast, I made sure to put it on real thick. Putting heat on the vinyl while streaching it really helped it keep it's shape.<P><BR>TwisT- You bet man. LMK when your in town.<P>------------------<BR>-Brian, Toolmaker<BR>Lincoln, NE<BR>85' SC & 87' GT-Leather, Lowered and On The Bottle<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=247832&a=7653930&p=37756786&Sequence=0"> ||||reg||1
